></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Hresko, M.C., L.A. Schriefer, P. Shrimankar, and R.H. Waterston. <year>1999</year>. Myotactin, a novel hypodermal protein involved in muscle-cell adhesion in <italic>Caenorhabditis elegans</italic>. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>146</volume>:<fpage>659</fpage>&#x02013;672.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10444073</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Hutter, H., B.E. Vogel, J.D. Plenefisch, C.R. Norris, R.B. Proenca, J. Spieth, C. Guo, S. Mastwal, X. Zhu, J. Scheel, and E.M. Hedgecock. <year>2000</year>. Conservation and novelty in the evolution of cell adhesion and extracellular matrix genes. <source>Science.</source> <volume>287</volume>:<fpage>989</fpage>&#x02013;994.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10669422</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Karabinos, A., H. Schmidt, J. Harborth, R. Schnabel, and K. Weber. <year>2001</year>. Essential roles for four cytoplasmic intermediate filament proteins in <italic>Caenorhabditis elegans</italic> development. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>98</volume>:<fpage>7863</fpage>&#x02013;7868.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11427699</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Labouesse, M. <year>1997</year>. Deficiency screen based on the monoclonal antibody MH27 to identify genetic loci required for morphogenesis of the <italic>Caenorhabditis elegans</italic> embryo. <source>Dev. Dyn.</source> <volume>210</volume>:<fpage>19</fpage>&#x02013;32.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9286592</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Lee, S., and P.A. Kolodziej. <year>2002</year>a. The plakin Short Stop and the RhoA GTPase are required for E-cadherin-dependent apical surface remodeling during tracheal tube fusion. <source>Development.</source> <volume>129</volume>:<fpage>1509</fpage>&#x02013;1520.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11880359</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Lee, S., and P.A. Kolodziej. <year>2002</year>b. Short Stop provides an essential link between F-actin and microtubules during axon extension. <source>Development.</source> <volume>129</volume>:<fpage>1195</fpage>&#x02013;1204.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11874915</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="journal">Leung, C.L., K.J. Green, and R.K. Liem. <year>2002</year>. Plakins: a family of versatile cytolinker proteins. <source>Trends Cell Biol.</source> <volume>12</volume>:<fpage>37</fpage>&#x02013;45.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11854008</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><citation citation-type="journal">Mackinnon, A.C., H. Qadota, K.R. Norman, D.G. Moerman, and B.D. Williams. <year>2002</year>. <italic>C. elegans</italic> PAT-4/ILK functions as an adaptor protein within integrin adhesion complexes. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>12</volume>:<fpage>787</fpage>&#x02013;797.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12015115</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><citation citation-type="journal">McDonald, K. <year>1999</year>. High-pressure freezing for preservation of high resolution fine structure and antigenicity for immunolabeling. <source>Methods Mol. Biol.</source> <volume>117</volume>:<fpage>77</fpage>&#x02013;97.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10327400</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib29"><citation citation-type="journal">McGrath, J.A., and R.A. Eady. <year>2001</year>. Recent advances in the molecular basis of inherited skin diseases. <source>Adv. Genet.</source> <volume>43</volume>:<fpage>1</fpage>&#x02013;32.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11037297</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib30"><citation citation-type="journal">McMahon, L., R. Legouis, J.L. Vonesch, and M. Labouesse. <year>2001</year>. Assembly of <italic>C. elegans</italic> apical junctions involves positioning and compaction by LET-413 and protein aggregation by the MAGUK protein DLG-1. <source>J. Cell Sci.</source> <volume>114</volume>:<fpage>2265</fpage>&#x02013;2277.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11493666</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib31"><citation citation-type="journal">Miller, D.M. III, I. Ortiz, G.C. Berliner, and H.F. Epstein. <year>1983</year>. Differential localization of two myosins within nematode thick filaments. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>34</volume>:<fpage>477</fpage>&#x02013;490.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6352051</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib32"><citation citation-type="journal">Misteli, T. <year>2001</year>. The concept of self-organization in cellular architecture. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>155</volume>:<fpage>181</fpage>&#x02013;185.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11604416</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib33"><citation citation-type="journal">Nievers, M.G., R.Q. Schaapveld, and A. Sonnenberg. <year>1999</year>. Biology and function of hemidesmosomes. <source>Matrix Biol.</source> <volume>18</volume>:<fpage>5</fpage>&#x02013;17.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10367727</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib34"><citation citation-type="journal">Nikolic, B., E. MacNulty, B. Mir, and G. Wiche. <year>1996</year>. Basic amino acid residue cluster within nuclear targeting sequence motif is essential for cytoplasmic plectin-vimentin network junctions. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>134</volume>:<fpage>1455</fpage>&#x02013;1467.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8830774</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib35"><citation citation-type="journal">Plenefisch, J.D., X. Zhu, and E.M. Hedgecock. <year>2000</year>. Fragile skeletal muscle attachments in dystrophic mutants of <italic>Caenorhabditis elegans</italic>: isolation and characterization of the <italic>mua</italic> genes. <source>Development.</source> <volume>127</volume>:<fpage>1197</fpage>&#x02013;1207.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10683173</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib36"><citation citation-type="journal">Priess, J.R., and D.I. Hirsh. <year>1986</year>. <italic>Caenorhabditis elegans</italic> morphogenesis: the role of the cytoskeleton in elongation of the embryo. <source>Dev. Biol.</source> <volume>117</volume>:<fpage>156</fpage>&#x02013;173.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3743895</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib37"><citation citation-type="journal">Prokop, A., J. Uhler, J. Roote, and M. Bate. <year>1998</year>. The <italic>kakapo</italic> mutation affects terminal arborization and central dendritic sprouting of <italic>Drosophila</italic> motorneurons. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>143</volume>:<fpage>1283</fpage>&#x02013;1294.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9832556</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib38"><citation citation-type="journal">Pulkkinen, L., and J. Uitto. <year>1999</year>. Mutation analysis and molecular genetics of epidermolysis bullosa. <source>Matrix Biol.</source> <volume>18</volume>:<fpage>29</fpage>&#x02013;42.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10367729</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib39"><citation citation-type="journal">Roper, K., S.L. Gregory, and N.H. Brown. <year>2002</year>. The &#x02018;Spectraplakins&#x02019;: cytoskeletal giants with characteristics of both spectrin and plakin families. <source>J. Cell Sci.</source> <volume>115</volume>:<fpage>4215</fpage>&#x02013;4225.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12376554</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib40"><citation citation-type="journal">Schnabel, R. <year>1995</year>. Duels without obvious sense: counteracting inductions involved in body wall muscle development in the <italic>Caenorhabditis elegans</italic> embryo. <source>Development.</source> <volume>121</volume>:<fpage>2219</fpage>&#x02013;2232.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7635065</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib41"><citation citation-type="journal">Schock, F., and N. Perrimon. <year>2002</year>. Molecular mechanisms of epithelial morphogenesis. <source>Annu. Rev. Cell Dev. Biol.</source> <volume>18</volume>:<fpage>463</fpage>&#x02013;493.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12142280</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib42"><citation citation-type="journal">Spence, H.J., Y.J. Chen, and S.J. Winder. <year>2002</year>. Muscular dystrophies, the cytoskeleton and cell adhesion. <source>Bioessays.</source> <volume>24</volume>:<fpage>542</fpage>&#x02013;552.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12111737</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib43"><citation citation-type="journal">Strumpf, D., and T. Volk. <year>1998</year>. Kakapo, a novel cytoskeletal-associated protein is essential for the restricted localization of the neuregulin-like factor, vein, at the muscle-tendon junction site. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>143</volume>:<fpage>1259</fpage>&#x02013;1270.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9832554</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib44"><citation citation-type="journal">Sun, D., C.L. Leung, and R.K. Liem. <year>2001</year>. Characterization of the microtubule binding domain of microtubule actin crosslinking factor (MACF): identification of a novel group of microtubule associated proteins. <source>J. Cell Sci.</source> <volume>114</volume>:<fpage>161</fpage>&#x02013;172.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11112700</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib45"><citation citation-type="journal">Williams, B.D., and R.H. Waterston. <year>1994</year>. Genes critical for muscle development and function in <italic>Caenorhabditis elegans</italic> identified through lethal mutations. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>124</volume>:<fpage>475</fpage>&#x02013;490.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8106547</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn id="fn1"><label>*</label><p>Abbreviations used in this paper: ABD, actin-binding domain&#x0003b; BPAG, bullous pemphigoid antigen&#x0003b; FO, fibrous organelle&#x0003b; GAR, growth-arrest protein 2&#x02013;related homology&#x0003b; IF, intermediate filament&#x0003b; MCAF, microtubule actin cross-linking factor&#x0003b; MF, microfilament&#x0003b; MT, microtubule&#x0003b; RNAi, RNA interference.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>